Two cars arriving at two gates simultaneously must not be assigned the same spot. Three viable approaches:

**1. Per-spot atomic check-and-set (recommended for in-memory):**
```java
public class Spot {
    private final SpotId id;
    private final SpotType type;
    private final AtomicReference<Vehicle> occupant = new AtomicReference<>();

    public boolean tryAssign(Vehicle v) {
        return occupant.compareAndSet(null, v);   // atomic
    }
    public void release() { occupant.set(null); }
    public boolean isFree() { return occupant.get() == null; }
}
```

The allocator iterates candidate spots and the first one whose `tryAssign` returns `true` wins. No lot-wide lock; lock-free per spot.

**2. Per-floor lock:** `synchronized` on each `Floor.findFree()`. Simpler but serializes all assignments on a floor.

**3. Distributed (Redis):** `SET spot:id NX` for cross-instance coordination. Bring this up only if the interviewer asks about distribution.

Approach 1 scales best for a single instance and is what you should pick by default.

```java
public class ParkingLot {
    private final List<Floor> floors;
    private final SpotAllocator allocator;
    private final FeeStrategy feeStrategy;
    private final TicketRepository tickets;
    private final Clock clock;

    public Ticket park(Vehicle v) {
        Spot s = allocator.allocate(floors, v)
            .orElseThrow(LotFullException::new);
        Ticket t = new Ticket(TicketId.next(), v, s, clock.instant());
        tickets.save(t);
        return t;
    }

    public Receipt unpark(TicketId id) {
        Ticket t = tickets.findById(id).orElseThrow(InvalidTicketException::new);
        Instant exit = clock.instant();
        Money amount = feeStrategy.calculate(t, exit);
        t.spot().release();
        tickets.remove(id);
        return new Receipt(t, exit, amount);
    }
}

public class NearestSpotAllocator implements SpotAllocator {
    @Override
    public Optional<Spot> allocate(List<Floor> floors, Vehicle v) {
        for (Floor f : floors) {                       // floors ordered by proximity to entry
            for (SpotType type : SpotType.compatibleWith(v.category())) {
                Optional<Spot> spot = f.findFree(type);
                if (spot.isPresent() && spot.get().tryAssign(v)) {
                    return spot;                       // wins the race
                }
            }
        }
        return Optional.empty();
    }
}

public class HourlyFeeStrategy implements FeeStrategy {
    private final Map<SpotType, Money> hourlyRates;

    @Override
    public Money calculate(Ticket t, Instant exit) {
        long minutes = Duration.between(t.entryTime(), exit).toMinutes();
        long hours = (minutes + 59) / 60;              // round up partial hour
        if (hours == 0) hours = 1;                     // minimum charge
        return hourlyRates.get(t.spot().type()).times(hours);
    }
}
```

Notice the `Clock` injection — testable without freezing real time.
